Article 11
(1) Services are implemented to fulfill the rights of women victims and are carried out with the following principles:
a. respect for human rights; b. non-discrimination;
c. confidentiality;
d. empathy;
e. inclusion;
f. empowerment;
g. best interests of the victim;
h. honesty;
i. professionalism;
j. integration; and
k. sustainability.
(2) Services to women victims must take into consideration special conditions and needs based on the vulnerability experienced by women as referred to in Article 7.
